"A sea cave opens in Gullrock Head's seaward foot, dry to walk into only at low tide."
"Low tide falls around dawn and again around dusk; at high tide the cave mouth is under the surf."
"At the back of the sea cave a stone arch carved with worn sea shapes leads down stairs into the dark."
"The arch is the way into the Salt Halls; the System names it when she first nears it."
